{"assertionId":"745f730a-d6c3-4191-9c43-ac89f198df78","entityBindings":[],"fragments":[{"exactText":"We used data from the Dunedin Study 1972–1973 birth cohort tracking within-individual decline in 19 indicators of organ-system integrity across four time points spanning two decades to model Pace of Aging. We distilled this two-decade Pace of Aging into a single-time-point DNA-methylation blood-test using elastic-net regression and a DNA-methylation dataset restricted to exclude probes with low test-retest reliability. We evaluated the resulting measure, named DunedinPACE, in five additional datasets.","fragmentId":"sha256:a21b68a9fea2a3b97e6bddb8400e899647c802ae419291285d68581fc970dca0"}],"proposition":"The paragraph describes a randomized intervention trial with only one measurement occasion.","qualifiers":[],"rubricVersion":"evidence-only.v1"}